# Exclusive QProcess ownership

`std::unique_ptr<QProcess>` is the only owner. Do not also pass `this` as a Qt parent. Never assign a new process while the previous one is still stored.

`stopAndDiscardProcess()` must `release()`, disconnect, kill/wait if running, then `deleteLater()`. Share that cleanup with the destructor. Do not `unique_ptr::reset()` on the `finished()` stack.

```cpp
// BAD — parented AND leaked on reuse; finished() can land on the next run
process_ = new QProcess(this);
process_->start(ffmpegPath, arguments);

// GOOD
stopAndDiscardProcess();
process_ = std::make_unique<QProcess>();
connect(process_.get(), &QProcess::finished, this, &Klass::onProcessFinished);
process_->start(ffmpegPath, arguments);
```
